IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 91 and subsections 104(1) and (2) -- THE DEFINITIONS OF PART III.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2628 to 2636 and 2723 to 2730 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 91 defines four words for Part III: the additional Canada Pension Plan, the base Canada Pension Plan, the
-- Investment Board and the Minister. Subsection 104(1) defines three words for sections 104, 104.1 and 105:
-- administration, federal institution and public officer; subsection 104(2) keeps them there.
--
-- The definitions of "base Canada Pension Plan" and "additional Canada Pension Plan" sort a portion of a benefit, and a
-- contribution in respect of it, into one of the two plans. The accounts module (cp6-accounts.l4) uses the sorting for the two
-- accounts of Canada.
--
-- "Investment Board" is inert (NOTES.md, coverage table): it names a body that another Act, which is not among the texts this
-- encoding reads, establishes. "Minister" is the core's enumeration Minister (the Minister of Employment and Social Development).
--
-- "Prescribed" in the definition of public officer is the core's section 2(1) "prescribed": a regulation must prescribe the
-- individual or the class. Regulation 37(4) (piece cr2) prescribes "a person employed in a federal institution or whose services are
-- required by a federal institution, on a casual or temporary basis or under a student employment program"; here that is a yes/no input.

§ `Part III -- definitions (section 91 and subsections 104(1) and (2))`

§§ `Section 91 -- additional Canada Pension Plan and base Canada Pension Plan`

-- out of range: paragraphs 46(1)(b) and (c) (piece cp3); subparagraphs 56(1)(b)(ii) and (iii), clauses 58(1)(a)(ii)(B) and (C) and (a.1)(ii)(B) and (C), subparagraphs 58(1)(b)(ii) and (iii) and subsections 59.1(3) and (5) (piece cp4).
-- They are only named here: the enumeration says which provision refers to the portion, and no rule of those provisions is read.
-- The twelve provisions that name the portions of benefits which make up the additional Canada Pension Plan, and a thirteenth
-- member for every other portion.
-- src:2630 | Interpretation
-- src:2631 | Definitions
-- src:2632 | 91 The following definitions apply in this Part.
-- src:2633 | additional Canada Pension Plan means the part of the Canada Pension Plan relating to the portions of benefits that are referred to in paragraphs 46(1)(b) and (c), subparagraphs 56(1)(b)(ii) and (iii), clauses 58(1)(a)(ii)(B) and (C) and (a.1)(ii)(B) and (C), subparagraphs 58(1)(b)(ii) and (iii) and subsections 59.1(3) and (5) and all contributions in respect of those portions of benefits. (régime de pensions supplémentaire du Canada)
@ref Act s 91 "additional Canada Pension Plan" (src:2630-2633)
DECLARE `cp6 Portion of a benefit named by the provision that refers to it` IS ONE OF
    `the portion referred to in paragraph 46(1)(b)`
    `the portion referred to in paragraph 46(1)(c)`
    `the portion referred to in subparagraph 56(1)(b)(ii)`
    `the portion referred to in subparagraph 56(1)(b)(iii)`
    `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a)(ii)(B)`
    `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a)(ii)(C)`
    `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a.1)(ii)(B)`
    `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a.1)(ii)(C)`
    `the portion referred to in subparagraph 58(1)(b)(ii)`
    `the portion referred to in subparagraph 58(1)(b)(iii)`
    `the portion referred to in subsection 59.1(3)`
    `the portion referred to in subsection 59.1(5)`
    `any other portion of a benefit`

@ref Act s 91 "additional Canada Pension Plan" (src:2633)
GIVEN portion IS A `cp6 Portion of a benefit named by the provision that refers to it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` portion MEANS
    CONSIDER portion
    WHEN `any other portion of a benefit` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Part of the base plan is whatever the additional plan does not include: "other than the portions ... that are
-- included in the additional Canada Pension Plan".
-- src:2634 | base Canada Pension Plan means the part of the Canada Pension Plan relating to benefits and contributions under this Act, other than the portions of those benefits and contributions that are included in the additional Canada Pension Plan. (régime de pensions de base du Canada)
@ref Act s 91 "base Canada Pension Plan" (src:2634)
GIVEN portion IS A `cp6 Portion of a benefit named by the provision that refers to it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` portion MEANS
    NOT (`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` portion)

-- "and all contributions in respect of those portions of benefits": a contribution in respect of one of those portions is
-- part of the additional plan; every other contribution under the Act is part of the base plan.
@ref Act s 91 "additional Canada Pension Plan" (src:2633)
GIVEN `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 — a contribution is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits` MEANS
    `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits`

@ref Act s 91 "base Canada Pension Plan" (src:2634)
GIVEN `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 — a contribution is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits` MEANS
    NOT (`s 91 — a contribution is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the contribution is in respect of one of those portions of benefits`)

§§ `Section 91 -- Minister`

-- src:2636 | Minister means the Minister of Employment and Social Development. (ministre)
@ref Act s 91 "Minister" (src:2636)
GIVETH A Minister
`s 91 — the Minister of Part III` MEANS `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`

§§ `Subsection 104(1) -- administration, federal institution, public officer`

-- "includes": the list is not closed, so an activity the list does not name is NOTHING, not FALSE (as for the core's "business").
-- src:2723 | Definitions
-- src:2724 | 104 (1) The following definitions apply in this section and sections 104.1 and 105.
-- src:2725 | administration includes the development, operation, evaluation and enforcement of policies and programs. (mise en oeuvre)
DECLARE `cp6 Kind of activity of the administration of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the development of policies and programs`
    `the operation of policies and programs`
    `the evaluation of policies and programs`
    `the enforcement of policies and programs`
    `another activity`

@ref Act s 104(1) "administration" (src:2723-2725)
GIVEN activity IS A `cp6 Kind of activity of the administration of the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104(1) — an activity is administration` activity MEANS
    CONSIDER activity
    WHEN `another activity` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2726 | federal institution means a department or any other body referred to in Schedule I, I.1, II or III to the Financial Administration Act. (institution fédérale)
@ref Act s 104(1) "federal institution" (src:2726)
GIVEN `the body is a department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is referred to in Schedule I, I.1, II or III to the Financial Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104(1) — a body is a federal institution` `the body is a department` `the body is referred to in Schedule I, I.1, II or III to the Financial Administration Act` MEANS
    -- the Financial Administration Act is not among the texts this encoding reads: the Schedules are a yes/no input
    `the body is a department` OR `the body is referred to in Schedule I, I.1, II or III to the Financial Administration Act`

-- src:2727 | public officer means an officer or employee of a federal institution, or a prescribed individual or a member of a prescribed class of individuals. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Act s 104(1) "public officer" (src:2727)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or employee of a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is one a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a class a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` `the person is an officer or employee of a federal institution` `the individual is one a regulation prescribes` `the person is a member of a class a regulation prescribes` MEANS
        `the person is an officer or employee of a federal institution`
    -- out of range: regulation 37(4) (piece cr2) prescribes the individuals; section 2(1) "prescribed" is the core's rule
    OR  `s 2(1) — prescribed` `any other matter` FALSE `the individual is one a regulation prescribes` FALSE
    OR  `s 2(1) — prescribed` `any other matter` FALSE `the person is a member of a class a regulation prescribes` FALSE

§§ `Subsection 104(2) -- the definitions stay where they are`

-- src:2728 | Interpretation
-- src:2729 | (2) The definition of a word or expression in subsection (1) does not affect its interpretation in any other provision of this Act.
@ref Act s 104(2) (src:2728-2729)
DECLARE `cp6 Provision of the Act in which a defined word appears` IS ONE OF
    `section 104`
    `section 104.1`
    `section 105`
    `any other provision of the Act`

@ref Act s 104(1), (2) (src:2724-2729)
GIVEN provision IS A `cp6 Provision of the Act in which a defined word appears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 104(2) — a definition in subsection 104(1) governs the provision` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `section 104` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 104.1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 105` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other provision of the Act` THEN FALSE

-- Subsection 104(3) (line 2730) is repealed in this text and states nothing.
